        "visual": false,
        "design_plan": false
      },
      "time": "",
      "narrative": "Tab 3\n\nThis is where the agent ledger comes in. I see my top movers, what my budget governance policies are, as well as my estimated spend.\n\nHere is the contract policy expert from before that Jessica made, it’s from Microsoft Foundry, using GPT 5.5, and it looks like we are way over budget.\n\nThat's not good.\n\nIn fact, as I scroll down, I can see these red indicators, and it looks like we’re going to hit our GPT 5.5 usage cap. There’s even a suggestion to route to a lower cost model.\n\nEarlier we saw from John how we needed to improve the agent performance, it looks like we also need to improve its cost.\n\nGuess what? I would’ve never caught this if it wasn’t for Agent 365 in the Microsoft Admin Center.\n\nAs a developer, I love that I’m able to observe my entire agentic estate, make decisions about what agents are available, to whom, and at what cost with Agent 365.",
      "demo_actions": "",
